      "rank": 2,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "Indirect Cooking Instructions"
      ],
      "section_title": "Indirect Cooking Instructions",
      "text": "## Indirect Cooking Instructions\n\nAlways cook with the lid closed. Due to weather conditions, cooking times may vary. During cold and windy conditions the temperature setting may need to be increased to ensure sufficient cooking temperatures.\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual19_37.jpg)\n\n2 Burner Cooking: Great indirect cooking on low. Produces slow, even heating. Ideal for slow roasting and baking.",
      "images": [
        "Manual19_37"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "General Grill Cleaning"
      ],
      "section_title": "General Grill Cleaning",
      "text": "## General Grill Cleaning\n\n- Keep the outside of your grill looking new by cleaning it once a month with warm soap and water or a non-abrasive cleaner. If you do not have a grill cover, wipe off dust and grime before starting your grill.\n- Coating the cooking grids with spray-on cooking oil will keep the food from sticking and make cleanup easier. After cooking, scrape the grates with a long-handled brass wire bristle brush.\n- Check inside the grill bottom for grease buildup and clean often, especially after cooking fatty meat.\n- Do not mistake brown or black accumulation of grease and smoke for paint. Apply a strong solution of detergent and water, or use a grill cleaner with a scrub brush on the insides of the grill lid and bottom. Rinse and allow to completely air dry. Do not apply a caustic grill or oven cleaner to painted surfaces.\n- **Plated wire grates:** Wash grates with concentrated grill cleaner or use soap and water solution. Dry thoroughly and store indoors between cookouts.\n- **Plastic parts:** Wash with warm soapy water and wipe dry. Do not use citrisol, abrasive cleaners, degreasers, or a concentrated grill cleaner on plastic parts. Damage to and failure of parts can result.\n- **Porcelain grates:** Because of glass-like composition, most residue can be wiped away with baking soda/water solution or specially formulated cleaner. Use non-abrasive scouring powder for stubborn stains.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "Safety Tips"
      ],
      "section_title": "Safety Tips",
      "text": "## Safety Tips\n\nBefore opening LP tank valve, check the coupling nut for tightness. When grill is not in use, turn off all control knobs and LP tank valve. Never move grill while in operation or still hot. Use long-handled barbecue utensils and oven mitts to avoid burns and splatters. Maximum load for shelves is 10 lbs. Do not use a cooking pot larger than 9\" on grid. The grease tray must be installed into opening in back panel and should be emptied after each use. Do not remove grease tray until grill has completely cooled. If you notice grease or other hot material dripping from grill onto valve, hose or regulator, turn off gas supply at once. Determine the cause, correct it, then clean and inspect valve, hose and regulator before continuing. Perform a leak test. The regulator may make a humming or whistling noise during operation. This will not affect safety or use of grill. If you have a grill problem, see the \"Troubleshooting Section\".\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual19_24.jpg)",
      "images": [
        "Manual19_24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "For Safe Use Of Your Grill And To Avoid Serious Injury"
      ],
      "section_title": "For Safe Use Of Your Grill And To Avoid Serious Injury",
      "text": "## For Safe Use Of Your Grill And To Avoid Serious Injury\n\n- Do not let children operate or play near grill\n\n- Keep grill area clear and free from materials that burn.\n\n- Do not block holes in bottom or back of grill\n\n- Check burner flames regularly\n\n- Use grill only in well-ventilated space. NEVER use in enclosed space such as carport, garage, porch, covered patio, or under an overhead structure of any kind.\n\n- Do not use charcoal or ceramic briquets in a gas grill! (Unless briquets are supplied with your grill)\n\n- Use grill at least 3 ft. from any wall or surface. Maintain 10 ft. clearance to objects that can catch fire or sources of ignition such as pilot lights on water heaters, live electrical appliances, etc.\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual19_23.jpg)",
      "images": [
        "Manual19_23"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

