{
  "content": "The Dual Mode Virtual Wall Barrier is an accessory that helps you keep the vacuum robot in areas you want cleaned and out of areas you don't want it to enter. It has two modes: Virtual Wall mode and Halo mode. In Virtual Wall mode, the device creates a linear barrier that can block openings up to 10 feet (3 meters), with the barrier widening as it gets farther from the device. In Halo mode, it creates a circular barrier about 12 inches (30 cm) from the center of the device, which is useful for protecting things like pet bowls, vases, or desks. Best results are achieved when the barrier is placed at least 8 feet (2.5 meters) from the Home Base.",
  "images": ["Manual32_4", "Manual32_6", "Manual32_5"]
}

small_answer.raw_response:
{
  "content": "1. Before starting, confirm the parking brake is applied and the engine stop switch is in the ON position. 2. Fully open the starter lever (choke). 3. For electric starting model: Turn the main switch to the START position. After the engine starts, set the starter lever to the Half-open position. Warm up the engine until it does not run roughly or begin to stall when the starter lever is returned to the Close position. Release the switch immediately after the engine starts. Do not crank the engine more than 10 seconds on any one attempt. 4. For manual starting model: Turn the main switch to the ON position. Pull slowly on the recoil starter until it is engaged, then pull it briskly. After the engine starts, warm up the engine until it does not run roughly or begin to stall when the starter lever is returned to the Close position. <PIC>",
  "images": ["Manual34_116"]
}

