      ],
      "section_title": "Steering",
      "text": "## Steering\n\nYour boat can be steered by turning the steering wheel the same direction you wish to travel, to the right or left. When the steering wheel is turned, the angle of the jet thrust nozzles at the rear of the craft is changed, and the change in direction of the jet thrust nozzles changes the direction of the boat accordingly. In addition, the direction of the articulating keel changes according to the movement of the jet thrust nozzles.\n\n1. Steering wheel\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual09_52.jpg)\n\n1. Jet thrust nozzle\n2. Articulating keel",
      "images": [
        "Manual09_52"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "doc_name": "Yamaha WaveRunner 2005",
      "header_path": [
        "2005 Yamaha WaveRunner Owner's Manual",
        "You need throttle to steer."
      ],
      "section_title": "You need throttle to steer.",
      "text": "## You need throttle to steer.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "doc_name": "Yamaha 210FSH 2021",
      "header_path": [
        "2021 Yamaha 210FSH Sport Deluxe Owner's Manual",
        "Steering"
      ],
      "section_title": "Steering",
      "text": "![Illustration](插图/Manual09_53.jpg)\n\nSince the strength of the jet thrust determines the speed and direction of a turn, the throttle must always be opened above idle when attempting a turn, except at trolling speed. Because boats steer from the stern, the sternot the boat swings out in the opposite direction of your turn. If you turn to starboard, for example, the sternot the boat will swing to the left. Keep this in mind when navigating near a person in the water, such as a down wake boarder or water-skier, or an obstacle, such as a dock.",
      "images": [
        "Manual09_53"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "doc_name": "Yamaha 210FSH 2021",
      "header_path": [
        "2021 Yamaha 210FSH Sport Deluxe Owner's Manual",
        "Turning the boat",
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "section_title": "WARNING",
      "text": "### WARNING\n\n Do not pull the remote control levers back to idle when trying to steer away from objects — you need throttle to steer.  Be sure passengers are holding on before making turns. An unprepared passenger could lose balance and fall. Steering control depends on the combinationot steering wheel position and the amount of throttle. Water sucked in through the intake grate is pressurized by the impeller in the jet pumps. As the pressurized water is expelled from the pumps through the jet thrust nozzles, it creates thrust to move and steer the boat. The higher the engine speed, the more thrust is produced. The amount of jet thrust, in addition to the positionot the steering wheel, determines how sharply you turn. A. More throttle produces high thrust, so the boat will turn more sharply.\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual09_239.jpg)",
      "images": [
        "Manual09_239"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

