big_answer.raw_response:
{
  "content": "Your boat steers by turning the steering wheel in the direction you want to go. This changes the angle of the jet thrust nozzles at the rear, which redirects the water jet and turns the boat. The articulating keel also moves with the nozzles to help with steering. <PIC> It's important to keep the throttle above idle (except at trolling speed) because the jet thrust determines the strength and direction of the turn. Also, remember that boats steer from the stern—the back of the boat swings out opposite to the turn direction. For example, turning to starboard makes the stern move left, so be cautious near obstacles or people in the water.",
  "images": ["Manual09_52", "Manual09_53"]
}

