small_answer.raw_response:
{
  "content": "To check the steering system while driving, first ensure the steering wheel is not loose and has no free play in-and-out or in rotation. Turn the steering wheel fully to the right and then fully to the left to verify smooth and unrestricted operation throughout the whole range. Watch the jet thrust nozzles at the rear of the boat: they must point to starboard (right) when the wheel is turned right, and to port (left) when turned left. There should be no free play between the steering wheel and the nozzles. Also confirm that the articulating keel moves in sync with the jet thrust nozzles. <PIC> Steering control requires throttle above idle; without thrust the boat will go straight even if the wheel is turned.",
  "images": ["Manual09_206"]
}

