To reduce the risk of fire, electrical shock, and injury to people;

- Use only a No. 26 AWG or larger telecommunication line cord.

small_answer.raw_response:
{
  "content": "1. Make sure the LP tank is properly secured on the grill, all control knobs are OFF, and the LP tank valve is OFF (turn OPD hand wheel clockwise to a full stop). 2. Remove the protective cap from the LP tank valve. 3. Hold the regulator and insert the nipple into the LP tank valve. Hand-tighten the coupling nut, keeping the regulator in a straight line with the valve to avoid cross-threading. The nipple must be centered in the valve. 4. Turn the coupling nut clockwise to a full stop, then tighten by hand an additional one-half to three-quarters turn. Do not use tools. 5. If you cannot complete the connection, disconnect and repeat steps 3 and 4. If still unable, do not use the regulator. <PIC>",
  "images": ["Manual19_19"]
}

