      "rank": 2,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "Leak Testing Valves, Hose and Regulator"
      ],
      "section_title": "Leak Testing Valves, Hose and Regulator",
      "text": "- Never attempt to attach this grill to the self-contained LP gas system of a camper trailer or motor home.\n\n- Do not use grill until leak-tested.\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual19_22.jpg)",
      "images": [
        "Manual19_22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "Safety Tips"
      ],
      "section_title": "Safety Tips",
      "text": "## Safety Tips\n\nBefore opening LP tank valve, check the coupling nut for tightness. When grill is not in use, turn off all control knobs and LP tank valve. Never move grill while in operation or still hot. Use long-handled barbecue utensils and oven mitts to avoid burns and splatters. Maximum load for shelves is 10 lbs. Do not use a cooking pot larger than 9\" on grid. The grease tray must be installed into opening in back panel and should be emptied after each use. Do not remove grease tray until grill has completely cooled. If you notice grease or other hot material dripping from grill onto valve, hose or regulator, turn off gas supply at once. Determine the cause, correct it, then clean and inspect valve, hose and regulator before continuing. Perform a leak test. The regulator may make a humming or whistling noise during operation. This will not affect safety or use of grill. If you have a grill problem, see the \"Troubleshooting Section\".\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual19_24.jpg)",
      "images": [
        "Manual19_24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "Valve Check"
      ],
      "section_title": "Valve Check",
      "text": "## Valve Check\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Make sure gas is off at the LP tank before checking valves. Knobs lock in the OFF position. To check valves, first push in the knobs and release; the knobs should spring back. If knobs do not spring back, replace the valve assembly before using the grill. Turn knobs to LO position, then turn back to OFF position. Valves should turn smoothly.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "doc_name": "Outdoor Grill",
      "header_path": [
        "Outdoor Grill Use and Care Guide",
        "LP Tank Leak Test For Your Safety"
      ],
      "section_title": "LP Tank Leak Test For Your Safety",
      "text": "## LP Tank Leak Test For Your Safety\n\n- Leak test must be repeated each time LP tank is exchanged or refilled.\n\n- Do not smoke during leak test.\n\n- Do not use an open flame to check for gas leaks.\n\n- Grill must be leak tested outdoors in a well-ventilated area, away from ignition sources such as gas-fired or electrical appliances. During leak test, keep grill away from open flames or sparks.\n\n- Use a clean paintbrush and a 50/50 mild soap and water solution. Brush soapy solution on to areas indicated by arrows in figure below. Leaks are indicated by growing bubbles.\n\n![Illustration](插图/Manual19_14.jpg)",
      "images": [
        "Manual19_14"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

