{
  "content": "Scan constantly for people, objects, and other watercraft. Operate defensively at safe speeds and keep a safe distance. Do not follow directly behind other watercraft. Do not spray or splash others. Avoid sharp turns or maneuvers that make it hard for others to avoid you. Avoid areas with submerged objects or shallow water. Never operate in water less than 90 cm (3 ft) deep for the 210FSH or less than 60 cm (2 ft) deep for WaveRunner models. Do not operate after sunset or before dawn if your watercraft is not equipped with lighting. Do not jump wakes or waves. Leave a float plan with a responsible person on shore. Take note of weather forecasts. Follow navigation rules and local laws. <PIC><PIC>",
  "images": ["Manual20_16", "Manual20_17"]
}

