small_answer.raw_response:
{
  "content": "Scan constantly for people, objects, and other watercraft. Be alert for conditions that limit your visibility. Operate defensively at safe speeds and keep a safe distance from people, objects, and other watercraft. Do not follow directly behind other watercraft. Do not go near others to spray or splash them with water. Avoid sharp turns or other maneuvers that make it hard for others to avoid you or understand where you are going. Avoid areas with submerged objects or shallow water. Never operate in water less than 60 cm (2 ft) deep (for Yamaha WaveRunner models) or less than 90 cm (3 ft) deep from the bottom of the boat (for Yamaha 210FSH models). Do not jump wakes or waves. Take early action to avoid collisions; boats do not have brakes. Do not pull the remote control lever back to idle when trying to steer away from objects—you need throttle to steer. Follow navigation rules and state and local laws. Check weather forecasts and prevailing conditions before setting out. Leave a float plan with a responsible person on shore. This watercraft is not equipped for night operation; do not operate after sunset or before dawn.",
  "images": []
}

