  "content": "The QSTS selector is a control located on the left handlebar grip of your WaveRunner. Its purpose is to adjust the trim angle of the watercraft by changing the vertical angle of the jet thrust nozzle. This lets you fine-tune how the bow sits in the water for different riding conditions. The QSTS selector has five positions: two bow-down positions, one neutral position, and two bow-up positions. To change the trim angle, you must first reduce engine speed to 3,000 r/min or less, then squeeze the shift lock lever, turn the QSTS selector to the desired position, and release the shift lock lever to lock it in place. <PIC> The image shows the QSTS selector and shift lock lever assembly on the handlebar. For further details on operation, see the “To change the trim angle” section of the manual.",
  "images": ["Manual20_34", "Manual20_51"]
}

