  "content": "To clean the intake and impeller, first ensure safety: stop the engine, remove the main switch key and engine shut-off cord (lanyard), and wait for all movement to stop. Then beach the watercraft. Inspect the jet intake and impeller for weeds, debris, or anything restricting water flow. If clogged, carefully remove the debris by hand or with a tool, being mindful of sharp impeller edges. Some models have an access port behind the rear platform hatch for easier cleaning. The illustration below shows the location of the intake and impeller. <PIC> For models with clean-out ports, follow the specific procedure to open the access cap and remove debris. <PIC> Always ensure the retaining cord is attached and the engine is off before reaching into the jet pump area.",
