  "content": "The grease filter should be removed and cleaned often, at least once a month. To remove the filter, slide it to the side, pull it downward, and push to the other side; it will drop out. <PIC> Clean the filter by washing it in the dishwasher or soaking it in hot water with a mild detergent. Rinse well and shake to dry. The manual cautions not to use ammonia or place the filter in a dishwasher, and notes that the aluminum filter will darken over time. <PIC> To reinstall, slide the filter into the side slot, then push up and toward the oven center to lock. <PIC>",
