small_answer.raw_response:
{
  "content": "To set the jumpers on a motherboard, locate the jumper block and place a jumper cap over the desired pins to change a setting. For example, the CPU Over Voltage jumper (3-pin CPU_OV) allows you to set a higher CPU voltage by inserting the jumper to pins 2-3, or return to default voltage by inserting it to pins 1-2. Another common jumper is the Clear RTC RAM jumper, which resets the motherboard to default values if the system fails to boot after BIOS changes. Always consult the motherboard manual for the exact jumper locations and pin configurations.",
  "images": []
}

