{
  "content": "Due to the memory address limitation on 32-bit, when you install 4GB or more memory on the motherboard, the actual usable memory for the OS can be about 3GB or less. For effective use of memory, use a maximum of 3GB system memory if using a 32-bit OS, or install a 64-bit OS if you want to install 4GB or more. You may install varying memory sizes in Channel A and Channel B; the system maps the total size of the lower-sized channel for dual-channel configuration, and excess memory from the higher-sized channel is mapped for single-channel operation. Always install DIMMs with the same CAS Latency, and use a 4-DIMM or 2-DIMM kit for full DIMM configuration. DIMM voltage below 1.65V is recommended to protect the CPU.",
  "images": []
}

