      "text": "27. Check the steam release valve, steam release pipe, anti-block shield, float valve, heating element, and air fryer lid element cover before and after use.\n28. Do not overfill the air fryer basket.\n29. Do not connect the appliance to an external timer switch or separate remote-control system.\n30. Use heat-resistant hand protection when removing accessories or handling the hot inner pot.\n31. While cooking, the internal temperature reaches several hundred degrees. Do not place unprotected hands inside the appliance until it has cooled.\n32. Keep hands and face away from air vents when the air fryer lid is operating.\n33. If the unit emits black smoke when using the air fryer lid, press `Cancel`, unplug the appliance, wait for smoke to stop, then clean thoroughly.\n34. Do not leave the appliance unattended while in use.\n35. Do not store materials in the cooker base or inner pot when not in use.\n36. Do not place combustible materials such as paper, cardboard, plastic, Styrofoam, or wood in the cooker base or inner pot.\n37. Do not use included accessories in a microwave, toaster oven, convection or conventional oven, ceramic cooktop, electric coil, gas range, or outdoor grill.\n38. Use caution when lifting a full inner pot.\n39. Use caution when removing the lid. Heat and steam escape as soon as the lid is removed.",
