big_answer.raw_response:
{
  "content": "Crossing a slope (side hill) requires proper weight distribution to maintain balance. The recommended technique is to lean your body uphill and adopt a kneeling position: place the knee of your downhill leg on the seat and the foot of your uphill leg on the running board. This allows you to shift weight as needed. If the snowmobile begins to slip sideways, steer in the direction of the slide (if no obstacles are present) and gradually steer back to your intended path as you regain balance. If the machine starts to tip, steer downhill to recover. If tipping is inevitable, dismount immediately on the uphill side. Note that side hills are not recommended for beginners. <PIC>",
  "images": ["Manual34_129"]
}

