{
  "content": "1. Remove the spark plug. 2. Inspect the color of the white porcelain insulator around the center electrode. The ideal coloration is a medium to light tan. A very white color may indicate an intake tract air leak or carburetion problem. 3. Measure the electrode gap with a wire thickness gauge and adjust to specification. 4. Before installing, clean the gasket surface and wipe off any grime from the threads. 5. Torque the spark plug to 28 Nm (2.8 m-kg, 20 ft-lb). 6. Use a spark plug with the correct reach (thread length). <PIC>",
  "images": ["Manual34_139"]
}

